# Words Folders says when it runs without the other parts of Trindle it sometimes needs.

folders-alone-no-share = Sharing a folder is set up by Trindle's own helper, which is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-mount = Opening a Windows share needs Trindle's own helper, which is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-nfs = Opening an NFS export needs Trindle's own helper, which is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-wallpaper = Setting the wallpaper needs Trindle's wallpaper program, which is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-root = Opening a folder as administrator needs pkexec, which is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-ai = Sharing with AI programs needs Trindle's program for them, which is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-terminal = No terminal is installed to open this folder in.
